  "caveats": [
    "Nucleon masses m_p, m_n are exact by construction: dressed quark masses μ_u, μ_d are solved from experimental CODATA values via the pair Skein formula. The deviations Δ arise solely from the limited precision of the constituent mass constants.",
    "Binding energies B/A from AME2020 are used as input. The deeper test is whether the nuclear Skein polynomial at q₀ reproduces these B/A values (confirmed for Z ≤ 92 via transfer matrix).",
    "For synthetic elements (Z ≥ 93), the q-torsion hypothesis predicts that Skein-derived B/A at q₀ may differ from AME2020 if nuclei were assembled at an effective q_eff > q₀."
  ]
}
